---
// src/components/ui/why-us-cards/InvoiceUnlockPreview.astro
//
// "Invoice paid -> automation rule -> files locked" workflow preview,
// ported from a user-supplied HTML/CSS reference
// (huzlly-payment-lock-preview.html): an invoice/paid trigger card,
// connected to an "If Paid -> Unlock Files" automation rule pill,
// connected (via a live/active emerald connector carrying a small
// spinning "processing" badge) to a locked-asset target card showing
// "Access Locked" / "Locked until client pays".
//
// Layout matches the original reference's branching/L-shaped canvas
// rather than a flat horizontal row: automation sits top-left, the
// trigger sits top-right (connected to automation via a bent
// up-then-left connector), and the locked-asset target sits bottom-left
// directly under automation (connected via a straight vertical
// connector carrying the processing badge). This is done with
// percentage-based absolute positioning for the three node boxes plus
// an inline SVG overlay (viewBox 0 0 100 100, preserveAspectRatio
// "none") for the two connector paths - the same idea as the original
// reference's %-positioned canvas + SVG connector overlay, just scaled
// down to fit inside this component's fixed-height box (h-32 sm:h-40 -
// see WhyUs.astro).
//
// Because every position is a percentage of the container (not a fixed
// px offset), this scales down proportionally at any width without a
// separate mobile breakpoint that restacks the nodes differently - it
// stays the same branching shape from the smallest width up, exactly
// like the previous flat layout stayed strictly horizontal at every
// width instead of restacking vertically.
//
// Node widths/paddings/font sizes are untouched from the previous
// version of this component - this is purely a positioning/connector
// change, not a content or styling-palette change. Automation sits
// noticeably shorter (a compact pill) than the trigger and target
// cards, which is what keeps the automation -> target vertical gap
// comfortable even inside the h-32 mobile box; see the delivery note
// for the fit-risk assessment at that height.
//
// Styling follows the established slate-900/slate-500/slate-200 +
// electric brand-blue base palette from ProposalFlowPreview.astro, with
// emerald kept as the semantic "paid / actively running" status color
// (paid badge + the live connector/processing badge) and amber kept as
// the semantic "locked / pending" status color for the target card -
// mirroring the reference's own --hf-emerald vs --hf-locked (amber)
// distinction, since neither concept exists in the sitewide token set
// and the reference relies on that color contrast to read correctly.
// The spinning processing icon is kept (Tailwind's built-in
// `animate-spin`, no custom CSS) since it's the visual detail that reads
// as "automation actively running" - the concept the whole card is
// selling.

export interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;
---

<div class:list={['relative h-full w-full', className]} aria-hidden="true">
  <!-- Connector overlay: trigger -> automation (bent, up-then-left) and
       automation -> target (straight vertical, live segment). Coordinate
       space is percentage-of-container on both axes (preserveAspectRatio
       "none"), matching the node positions below 1:1. Sits behind the
       node boxes (z-0) so line ends simply run under the opaque node
       backgrounds instead of needing to be trimmed to exact edges. -->
  <svg
    class="absolute inset-0 z-0 h-full w-full"
    viewBox="0 0 100 100"
    preserveAspectRatio="none"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
    <!-- trigger's RIGHT edge (vertical center) squiggling into automation:
         a cubic Bezier with two control points placed to create a genuine
         two-bend "S"/squiggle rather than one uniform bow - it leaves the
         trigger's right edge curving up and to the left (control point 1,
         pulled up and left of the start), then bends the opposite way,
         dipping back down before finally rising up and to the left into
         automation (control point 2, pulled down and right of the end
         point) - matching the hand-drawn reference sketch's squiggle shape.
         Start point is the trigger's right edge: trigger is centered at
         left-[80%] with a fixed sm:w-[92px] box, so its right edge sits at
         80% plus half that width as a percentage of this preview box's
         actual rendered width - not a fixed 68/92px offset, since this
         SVG's coordinate space is percentage-of-container while the node
         width is a fixed px value. Using the real WhyUs.astro grid math
         (max-w-6xl container, lg:grid-cols-5 + lg:gap-12, inner
         sm:grid-cols-2 + gap-5, Card.astro's p-6), the preview box renders
         at ~273px wide at a representative desktop width, putting the
         trigger's right edge at 80 + (46/273 * 100) ≈ 97 on this 0-100
         scale. End point (26,24) - visually into automation - is unchanged
         from before.

         NOTE on stroke rendering (bug fix): this path intentionally does
         NOT use vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke", unlike the
         automation -> target path below. That attribute, combined with
         this SVG's non-uniform scale (preserveAspectRatio="none" on a
         viewBox that's stretched much wider than tall to fill a ~273x160
         box), hits a known cross-engine SVG rendering edge case where a
         diagonal/curved non-scaling-stroke path fails to compute its
         render box and simply doesn't paint - while a purely
         axis-aligned line (like the straight vertical connector below)
         is unaffected, since its screen-space box under a non-uniform
         scale stays well-defined. That's exactly why only this curve
         went invisible while the vertical dashed line kept rendering
         fine. Fix: drop vector-effect here and pre-compensate
         stroke-width (0.75 instead of 1.5) so that once the SVG's own
         non-uniform scale stretches the stroke back out, the rendered
         thickness still lands close to the intended ~1.5px/1.5-unit
         line weight used elsewhere in this overlay. -->
    <path
      d="M 97 50 C 85 20 45 55 26 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="0.75"
      class="text-slate-300"
    />
    <!-- automation (26,24) straight down into target (26,74) -->
    <path
      d="M 26 24 L 26 74"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="1.5"
      stroke-dasharray="4 3"
      vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
      class="text-emerald-500/60"
    />
  </svg>

  <!-- Node 2: Automation rule (top-left) -->
  <div class="absolute left-[26%] top-[24%] z-10 flex w-[70px] shrink-0 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 items-center gap-0.5 rounded-full border border-slate-200 bg-white px-1.5 py-1 shadow-sm sm:w-[96px] sm:gap-1 sm:px-2 sm:py-1.5">
    <span class="flex h-3 w-3 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-50 text-electric sm:h-4 sm:w-4">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" class="h-1.5 w-1.5 sm:h-2.5 sm:w-2.5">
        <path d="M13 2 3 14h7l-1 8 10-12h-7l1-8z"/>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col">
      <span class="text-[5.5px] font-semibold uppercase leading-none tracking-wide text-slate-400 sm:text-[6.5px]">Automation</span>
      <span class="mt-0.5 line-clamp-2 text-[6px] font-semibold leading-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-[8px]">If Paid &rarr; Unlock Files</span>
    </span>
  </div>

  <!-- Node 1: Trigger (top-right, Invoice paid) -->
  <div class="absolute left-[80%] top-[50%] z-10 flex w-[68px] shrink-0 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex-col rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white px-1.5 py-1 shadow-sm sm:w-[92px] sm:rounded-xl sm:px-2 sm:py-1.5">
    <span class="text-[5.5px] font-bold uppercase leading-none tracking-wide text-slate-400 sm:text-[7px]">Trigger</span>
    <span class="mt-0.5 truncate text-[7px] font-semibold leading-tight text-slate-900 sm:mt-1 sm:text-[9px]">Invoice #1084</span>
    <span class="truncate text-[6px] font-medium leading-tight text-slate-500 sm:text-[7.5px]">$1,850.00</span>
    <div class="mt-1 border-t border-slate-100 pt-1 sm:mt-1.5 sm:pt-1.5">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 px-1 py-[1.5px] text-[6px] font-semibold text-emerald-600 sm:px-1.5 sm:py-[2px] sm:text-[7.5px]">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-[5px] w-[5px] shrink-0 sm:h-[7px] sm:w-[7px]">
          <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
        </svg>
        Paid
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Processing badge: sits on the automation -> target segment -->
  <span class="absolute left-[26%] top-[49%] z-10 flex h-3 w-3 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-emerald-200 bg-white shadow-sm sm:h-4 sm:w-4">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 animate-spin text-emerald-600 sm:h-2 sm:w-2">
      <polyline points="23 4 23 10 17 10"/>
      <polyline points="1 20 1 14 7 14"/>
      <path d="M3.51 9a9 9 0 0 1 14.85-3.36L23 10M1 14l4.64 4.36A9 9 0 0 0 20.49 15"/>
    </svg>
  </span>

  <!-- Node 3: Target outcome (bottom-left, locked asset) -->
  <div class="absolute left-[26%] top-[74%] z-10 flex w-[90px] shrink-0 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex-col rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-white px-1.5 py-1 shadow-md sm:w-[124px] sm:rounded-xl sm:px-2 sm:py-1.5">
    <div class="flex items-start gap-0.5 sm:gap-1">
      <span class="relative flex h-3 w-3 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-[5px] bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 sm:h-4 sm:w-4 sm:rounded-md">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-1.5 w-1.5 sm:h-2.5 sm:w-2.5">
          <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="10" rx="2"/>
          <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="absolute -bottom-[2px] -right-[2px] flex h-[7px] w-[7px] items-center justify-center rounded-[3px] border border-amber-200 bg-white text-amber-600 sm:h-2 sm:w-2">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="h-[5px] w-[5px] sm:h-[6px] sm:w-[6px]">
            <path d="M3 7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4l2 2h8a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v8a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V7z"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </span>
      <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <span class="block truncate text-[6.5px] font-bold leading-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-[8.5px]">Brand_Assets_Final.zip</span>
        <span class="mt-0.5 block truncate text-[5.5px] font-semibold leading-none text-amber-600 sm:text-[7px]">Access Locked</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-1 flex items-center gap-0.5 border-t border-slate-100 pt-1 sm:mt-1.5 sm:gap-1 sm:pt-1.5">
      <span class="h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-amber-500 sm:h-1.5 sm:w-1.5"></span>
      <span class="truncate text-[5.5px] font-semibold leading-none text-slate-500 sm:text-[7px]">Locked until client pays</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
